-- title:
--   Valuation subring meets FracB in B_P for nodal ̂ B
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a Noetherian local domain, and let $W$ be a domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to its maximal ideal; let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible and $E \ge 1$ a natural number. Suppose given a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $B$ at its maximal ideal onto the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^E$. Let $F$ be a field, $\mathrm{emb} : B \to F$ an injective ring homomorphism, and $V \subseteq F$ a valuation subring with $\mathrm{emb}(b) \in V$ for all $b \in B$. Let $P$ be an ideal of $B$ which is the centre of $V$, in the sense that $b \in P$ holds exactly when $\mathrm{emb}(b)$ is a non-unit of $V$, and assume $P$ is not the maximal ideal of $B$. The conclusion is that for every $x \in F$ lying in $V$ which can be written as a fraction over $\mathrm{emb}(B)$, i.e. $x\,\mathrm{emb}(s_0) = \mathrm{emb}(r_0)$ for some $r_0, s_0 \in B$ with $s_0 \ne 0$, there are $r, s \in B$ with $s \notin P$ and $x\,\mathrm{emb}(s) = \mathrm{emb}(r)$.
--
--   This is the statement that, for a Noetherian local domain whose completion is the nodal (uv-crossing) model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$, a valuation subring of an extension field whose centre $P$ on $B$ is not the closed point already contains no more of $\operatorname{Frac} B$ than the localisation $B_P$: every element of $V$ that is a fraction over $B$ is a fraction with denominator outside $P$. It serves the dictionary for tubes on a node annulus, where $V$ is the valuation ring of a boundary component and $P$ the kernel of the corresponding character.
